+- Without a pending start signal, new, paused and down checks keep that status; an up check is `up` until its next expected ping, `grace` during the grace time after it, and `down` afterwards. (`hc/api/tests/test_check_model.py` "test_status_works_with_cron_syntax")
+- The next expected ping is the last ping plus the period for a simple check, or the next scheduled time after the last ping, in the check's time zone, for a cron or OnCalendar check; a schedule that never fires again keeps the check `up`. (`hc/api/tests/test_check_model.py` "test_status_handles_stopiteration")
+- A check that received a start signal and no completion is `down` once the start is older than the grace time, whatever its stored status, paused and new included. (`hc/api/tests/test_check_model.py` "test_get_status_handles_paused_then_started_and_expired")
+- `grace` is never stored (the stored statuses are new, up, down and paused) and reading changes nothing, so the answer does not depend on the alert process running. (`hc/api/models.py` `STATUSES`)
